            <ArticleTitle>Pharmaco-toxicological effects of acetaminophen in rodents. Battery of tests to screen potential analgesic acetaminophen derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The pharmacological effects of acute oral administration of acetaminophen have been extensively evaluated in rodents. Using this drug as reference compound we have also standardized several pharmaco-toxociological tests in order to select new analgesic-antipyretic acetaminophen derivatives. According to the results obtained in this work, the following battery of assays is proposed to screen these compounds: a) pharmacological: antipyretic activity against Brewer's yeast-induced pyresis in rats; analgesic activity against chemical-induced writhings in mice and paw pressure test in rats; b) toxicological: oral acute toxicity in mice with and without phenobarbital pretreatment; determination of SGOT and SGPT activities as well as total bilirubin in mice. The usefulness of this procedure in the evaluation of drug effects is also considered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
